fL Folio\nSee all\nSchool of Medicine\nIntranet\nPatient Care\nNews & Events\nSite Search\nSchool of Medicine\nAll of UofL\nSearch\nSearch\nClose Search Tray\nAbout\nOur People\nQuick Facts\nLeadership & Organization\nOffices\nAccreditation\nHistory & Mission\nCareers\nAdmissions\nAuD Program Admissions\nBachelor's Degree Admissions\nMaster's Programs Admissions\nMD Program Admissions\nPhD Program Admissions\nAcademics & Programs\nAcademic Departments\nAudiology Academics & Programs\nMaster's Program\nMD Program\nPhD Programs\nDual Degree Programs\nResidency & Fellowship Programs\nPathways to Medicine\nLearner Experience\nResearch\nResearch Priorities\nRecognized Research\nCenters & Institutes\nResearch Labs & Groups\nResearch Programs\nFunding & Partnerships\nCommunity\nAHEC - Homepage\nOur Impact\nOutreach & Programs\nGet Involved\nAlumni & Friends\nBreadcrumb\nHome\n.....\nHome\nSOMAdmissions\nPhD Program \u2013 Admissions\nPhD Program \u2013 Admissions\nApply Now\nSidebar\nIn this section\nAdmissions\nAuD Program Admissions\nBachelor's Degree Admissions\nMaster's Programs Admissions\nMD Program Admissions\nPhD Program Admissions\nContact Us\nContact Us\nOffice of Graduate and Postdoctoral Studies\nOffice of Graduate and Postdoctoral Studies\nWebsite\nabout\nPhone:\n502-852-3740\nLocation:\n500 South Preston Street\nResearch Tower, Room 313\nLouisville, KY 40202\nHours:\nMonday - Friday\n8 a.m. to 5 p.m.\nEmail:\nogpds@louisville.edu\nThe University of Louisville, an R1-designated Research University, offers PhD studies across five basic biomedical discipline-based programs at the School of Medicine. Located at the heart of Louisville\u2019s medical district, the School of Medicine integrates academic rigor with real-world clinical experiences, preparing students to meet the complex needs of varied patient populations.\nStudents collaborate closely with distinguished faculty in the School of Medicine, gaining access to a wide range of exceptional research opportunities. Admission to these doctoral programs opens the door to cutting-edge research in both basic science laboratories and interdisciplinary work within clinical departments and research centers.\nOur holistic admissions process considers more than academic excellence \u2013 we value life experiences, leadership potential and a demonstrated commitment to service and impact.\nFrequently Asked Questions\nApplication Process\nPlease visit the Graduate School website for details about the application process.\nPrerequisites\nBachelor\u2019s degree or above.\nCompleted a curriculum including course work in appropriate scientific disciplines.\nMinimum GPA of 3.0\nFunding\nStudents admitted to one of the School of Medicine\u2019s PhD Programs receive a comprehensive 23-month fellowship that includes:\nFull-tuition coverage\nHealth insurance\nFollowing this initial fellowship period, continued funding is provided through support from the student\u2019s faculty mentor, department or external research grants.\nExperience the UofL difference\nAccreditation\nVirtual Tour\nLife in Louisville\nImportant Admissions Dates\nJanuary 15\nApplication Deadline\nAll completed applications for the PhD Program must be submitted no later than January 15.\nApril 15\nAcceptance of Offer Deadline\nDeadline for students to accept their fellowship offer is no later than April 15.\nSuccess By The Numbers\n125\nGraduate enrollment\n5\nBioMedical PhD programs\n169\nScholarly publications\nTop\nContact Us\nMore Contact Info\nabout\nEmail:\nmeddean@louisville.edu\nLocation:\nAbell Administration Building\nAddress:\n323 E. Chestnut St.\nLouisville, KY 40202\nConnect with School of Medicine\nfacebook\ntwitter\ninstagram\nlinkedin\nCommunity\nIntranet\nResearch\nGive Now\n\u00a9 2026 University of Louisville\nAccessibility\nAccreditation\nAlerts\nConsumer Information\nPrivacy\nTitle IX", "links": [["Skip to main content", "https://medicine.louisville.edu/SOMAdmissions/phd-program-admissions#main"], [""